# Sanity conventions (cms layer)

**Before schema or query work:** Sanity MCP `list_sanity_rules`, then load `schema`, `groq`,
`nextjs`, `page-builder`, `typegen`, `seo`, `image` in one call. Those are the official rules; this
file adds the Thrio house rules.

## Shape

```
studio/    standalone Sanity Studio (Vite). `sanity deploy` → <slug>.sanity.studio
web/       Next.js static export. Fetches Sanity at build time.
```

Never embed the Studio in Next.js (`docs/adr/0002`). One `projectId`, dataset `production`.
The client's email owns the Sanity project; Thrio is admin.

## Content model (confirm in `plan.md` before schema code)

- `page` with `sections[]` (page builder, 6–10 block types at launch), `siteSettings` singleton
  (nav, footer, NAP, social, default SEO), shared `seo` object. Collections only when `plan.md` lists them.
- Model **what things are**, not how they look. `features`, not `threeColumnRow`.
- `defineType` / `defineField` / `defineArrayMember` always; an icon from `@sanity/icons/<Name>` on every type.
- Objects by default; references only for content shared across pages. Every block has a `preview`.
- Editorial content only. Tokens, layout, nav structure, secrets stay in code. Forms never write to Sanity.
- Never delete a field with production data: deprecate → readOnly → hidden → migrate → remove.

## Fetching (static export)

- `web/src/sanity/client.ts` with `useCdn: false` for builds; all GROQ in `queries.ts` with
  `defineQuery`; always project `_key` on arrays.
- `generateStaticParams` from a slugs query; `perspective: "published"`.
- `sanity typegen generate` after every schema or query change; components type from
  `PAGE_QUERYResult`. No hand-written content types.
- Page builder renders by `switch (block._type)`; React `key={block._key}`.
- Heading levels come from the component's position, never from the schema.
- Publish → webhook → rebuild (`code-cloudflare.mdc` → Deploy). No Live Content API, no draft
  preview in a static export; if the client needs live preview, that is a server site (OpenNext).

## Images

Sanity CDN with `@sanity/image-url`; `alt` required in the schema; hotspot on; `next/image` with
the Sanity loader and an explicit aspect ratio per usage.
